WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.580
- Legal Eagle is coming in loud

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.630
and clear thanks to Ting Mobile.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.240
Neither snow nor rain nor heat nor gloom

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.700
of night stays postal
workers from their jobs

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.400
but they never met President Donald Trump.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.470
And now is there a postal conspiracy

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.750
to slow down mail to
affect the 2020 election.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.510
2020 will go down in
history as a year dominated

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.240
by the coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.460
But in case you haven't noticed,

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.180
we also have a major election coming up

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.800
in just a few short months

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.850
and COVID-19 spreads easily between people

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.520
who are in close contact endorsed

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.480
so states are scrambling for alternatives

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.840
to packing people into
polling places like sardines

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.800
and people are worried so
this has led to a shortage

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.070
of poll workers.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.070
The best solution according

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.500
to the Centers for Disease Control

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.360
is to increase voting by mail.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.930
And I have an entire video
devoted to voting by mail

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.150
and the potential for mail
fraud if there is one.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.120
But consistent with the
CDC's recommendation,

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.250
several states have expanded
the ability of voters

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.060
to vote absentee or by mail.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.230
As a result of these changes,

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.810
a record 76% of American
voters will be eligible

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.350
to receive a ballot in the mail

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.400
for the November 2020 election.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.700
Now it's not entirely
clear because he flip-flops

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:05.860
but it appears that President Trump

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.520
is against voting by mail.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.910
- [Donald] Now they
need that money in order

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.270
to have the post office work.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.470
So it can take all of
these millions and millions

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.060
of ballots but if they
don't get those two items,

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.010
that means you can't have
universal mail and voting.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.412
- And we can only speculate
as to why that is.

00:01:21.412 --> 00:01:22.990
And into this mess,

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.100
jumped new postmaster General Louis DeJoy.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.870
The man with the surname that sounds like

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.270
it should be a candy bar
is making sweeping changes

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.890
at the postal service.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.610
These changes include reducing staff,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.780
taking away blue mailboxes,
prohibiting overtime

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.423
and raising postage on ballots

00:01:37.423 --> 00:01:39.510
and throwing away mail sorters

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.520
which this reporter caught on video.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.640
- We are at the USPS, Patterson
location where behind me,

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.920
you can see a graveyard
of mail sorting pieces.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.410
They're just large pieces of machinery

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.480
that had been yanked out.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.700
In addition to that, there's
also a dumpster right there.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.333
And according to an employee
that works across the way

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:04.040
they tell me that that dumpster
has been billed three times

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.749
since last week with parts and pieces

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:11.300
of what we're being told are
the mail sorting machines.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.550
- The postal service has now warn

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.650
that states may not be
able to deliver ballots

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.440
in time for the November
election or deliver the ballots

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.050
that are in fact cast.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.920
And despite the fact that
President Trump has tweeted

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:24.390
that we should save the post
office, though not recognizing

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.240
that he is sort of the guy in charge.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.689
It appears that President Trump is opposed

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:31.420
to increasing funding for the
USPS and ensuring that ballots

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.110
are delivered on time.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.233
Coincidence or conspiracy?

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.780
Hey, Legal Eagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.480
because the USPS may hang in the balance.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.440
Today we're gonna take a
close look at what's happening

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.890
at the postal services.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.220
Louis DeJoy deliberately
trying to impact the outcome

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.070
of the election by slowing down the mail.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.928
And if so, can he be stopped?

00:02:53.928 --> 00:02:56.480
But first let's talk
about the actual structure

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.030
of the US post office.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.120
The USPS delivers 40% of the world's mail.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.820
However, COVID-19 caused
a significant reduction

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.230
in letter mail which is the
most profitable mail process

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:07.330
by the post office.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.290
And the COVID-19 crisis
could not have happened

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.470
at a worst time for the us post office.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.420
The volume of letter
mail has been decreasing

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.130
for quite some time mostly due
to the availability of email

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.350
and other options for
communicating quickly.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.170
To understand the current
issues we have to review

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.910
the basic legal structure
of the US post office.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.610
The post office was established in 1775

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.230
and the US post office was
actually a cabinet level agency

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.440
until 1970 when Congress passed

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.040
the Postal Reorganization
Act which established

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.710
the United States Postal Service

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.670
as a quasi independent
self funded organization.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.070
President George W. Bush signed
the Postal Accountability

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.690
and Enhancement Act in 2006.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:46.050
The PAEA was the first broad
revision of the 1970 statute.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.940
The PAEA imposed several new requirements

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.480
on how the postal service is allowed

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.040
to conduct it's business.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.770
Section 101 of the PAEA
a defines postal service

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.920
to mean the delivery of
letters, printed matter

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.980
or mailable packages

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.000
including acceptance collection sorting,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.050
transportation or other
functions ancillary there to.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.380
This section of the law
clarifies and limits

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.020
what the postal service can do.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.440
Prior to this law, the post office used

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.670
to sell things like prepaid
phone cards for example

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.800
but this practice ended after the payout

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.760
because the sale of prepaid phone cards

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.430
did not fit within this definition.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.660
This was good news for the
post office competitors

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.920
but bad news for the post
office's ability to self fund.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.550
And section 102 of the law
is a blanket prohibition

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.610
on new products that aren't mail.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.690
Several postmaster
generals have complained

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.070
that the postal service isn't permitted

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.630
to legally offer banking,
cell phone logistics

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.680
and other services the postal services

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.230
and other countries use to
generate the income necessary

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.250
to offset the cost of their
universal service obligation.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.060
Senator Bernie Sanders has suggested

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.360
that the post office be allowed

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.130
to provide basic banking services.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.297
- Postal service can make
billions of dollars a year

00:04:46.297 --> 00:04:49.680
by establishing basic banking services.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.830
So lower income people have access.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.130
- But this can't happen without
congressional intervention.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.360
Under title two of the
PAEA, the postal service

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.610
can only offer two categories of products,

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.120
market dominant products
and competitive products.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.260
The postal services
market dominant products

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.570
include things like
first class mail letters,

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.810
first class mail cards and media mail.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.360
With these monopolistic products,

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.930
the USPS can only increase
prices in accordance

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:14.610
with the consumer price index.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.390
This keeps the rates down for consumers

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:19.100
but contributes to the
postal services insolvency.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.400
But given the USPS has a
monopoly on these products,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.780
there's a reason why you don't
necessarily want the prices

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.280
to increase too dramatically.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:26.960
But competitive products include those

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.669
for which a competitive
market already exists.

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:31.890
Those include things like
priority mail, expedited mail

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.450
and bulk parcel post.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:34.780
For these competitive products,

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.400
the post office is barred from
offering prices lower than

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.660
the cost of delivery.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:42.430
So this means that the USPS
can't undercut FedEx and USPS

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:44.110
by offering dramatically lower prices

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.410
that are below the cost
of actually delivering.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.990
And again, this benefits consumers

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.410
but hurts the post office's
ability to fund itself

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.020
or offer lost leaders.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.440
The PAEA also established

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.120
the postal service retiree
health benefits fund.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.550
Section 801 to 803 of the
PAEA had changed the USPS

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.830
from funding its retirees healthcare costs

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:05.440
on a pay as you go basis to
pre-funding these obligations.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.350
The upshot of this is that
the post office had to create

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:10.040
a $72 billion fund to pay for the cost

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.940
of its post retirement health care cost.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.440
And the fact that the postal
service has to pre-fund

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.830
its retirement obligations
from a separate account,

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.570
hampers its financial prospects

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.610
and this pre-funding burden applies

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.640
to no other federal agency
and no private employer.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.980
Now the PAEA also created the
Postal Regulatory Commission.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:29.680
Now the PRC, no relation,
has significant powers

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.330
but it also has to follow the requirements

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.400
of the Administrative
Procedures Act or APA.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.420
We've talked about the
APA a lot on this channel

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.410
but it governs the process

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.680
by which federal agencies
develop regulations.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.860
It includes requirements
for publishing notices

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.620
of proposed and final rulemaking
in the federal register

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:45.300
and provides opportunities for the public

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.090
to comment on notices
of proposed rulemaking.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.730
The APA also requires most rules

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:52.010
to have a 30 day delayed effective date.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.250
The APA provides standards
for judicial review

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.160
if a person has been adversely affected

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.831
or aggrieved by an agency.

00:06:57.831 --> 00:07:01.000
So if the postal rate commission
maybe sweeping changes

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.720
without following the
APA and spoiler alert,

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.930
they did these changes
could be rolled back

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.150
by a federal court.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.750
And as an aside, a lot of people ask

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.320
why doesn't the postal
service run like a business.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.210
And many people have
argued that the post office

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:14.900
isn't profitable, they claim that

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:18.040
if it was any other business
like the Trump Taj Mahal

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:19.290
it would have declared bankruptcy

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.030
because it couldn't turn a profit.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.330
And in fact, Trump appointee
Richard Grinnell says that

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.180
the post office should
just charge you a lot more

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:27.940
to send letters and packages
to make the USPS profitable.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.340
And Senator Rand Paul
says that rural citizens

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.870
such as many of the people
that he represents in Kentucky

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.130
should just settle for receiving

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:35.530
the mail just three days a week.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.550
And those changes could help make

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.060
the postal service more profitable.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.250
But the postal service has legal mandate

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:44.070
to provide universal
service to all US addresses

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:47.000
without charging more for
more costly delivery routes.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:47.833
And this is known

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:51.030
as the Universal Service
Obligation or USO.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.660
The USO is not clearly
defined in legislation

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:56.100
but it's pieced together from
numerous laws and regulations.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.930
And the basic obligations
of the postal service

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:01.510
are defined in 39 USC
sections 101 and 403.

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:03.130
These statutes require the post office

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.010
to provide a range of product offerings,

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.170
maintain uniform prices and availability,

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:08.890
provide efficient services to people

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.070
in every geographic location in the US

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.440
and make its facilities
accessible to everyone.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.380
Congress gave the post office
a monopoly on mail service

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.860
in exchange for providing
all of these service benefits

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:22.350
to the American people uniformly
in both price and service.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:26.170
And under 39 USC section
404D, small post offices

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:29.590
may not be closed solely
for operating at a deficit.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:31.350
If the post office was legally allowed

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:32.824
to operate like any other business,

00:08:32.824 --> 00:08:35.970
it could eliminate thousands
of unprofitable post offices

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:39.180
in rural areas, it could cut
services to rural citizens,

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.840
it could only deliver the
mail three days a week

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:45.240
and it can charge much more
for different service routes.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.970
Now like many crises during the Trump era,

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.340
these problems began long

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.370
before President Trump took office

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:53.460
but the President has
exploited some of these issues

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:54.860
and accelerated them.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:57.390
The board of governors of
the USPS is responsible

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.780
for overseeing the activities
of the postal service

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:02.070
while the postmaster
general actively manages

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:03.500
its day to day operations.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.280
A postmaster general is not
appointed by the president

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.780
instead the board of
governors chooses a new person

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.320
only when there's a vacancy
and the board of governors

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.870
is designed to be as
nonpartisan as possible.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:15.780
For this reason, no more than five members

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.040
can be members of the
same political party.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.030
However, right now there
are only six members

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.930
of the board of governors
and all six of them

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.680
were appointed by President Trump.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.820
The other vacancies have not been filled,

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.910
presumably because
President Trump is required

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:29.780
by law to appoint Democrats.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.810
The board of governors
has not been fully staffed

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:35.030
since 2010 because
Senate Republicans refuse

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.810
to confirm five nominees
by President Obama.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.483
In April, the USPS notified Congress

00:09:39.483 --> 00:09:41.040
that it was running out of money

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.420
and in May, Repubican donor Louis DeJoy

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:46.460
was named postmaster general
by the now six members

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.880
of the board of governors.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:50.270
President Trump asked his
nominees who were the only people

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:52.300
on the board to appoint DeJoy.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.540
They did so despite his lack of experience

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:55.610
at the postal service,

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.760
he is the first postmaster general ever

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.060
to have zero experience with the USPS.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:01.940
He was most recently
the financial chairman

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.760
of the Republican National Committee.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.620
DeJoy hasn't divested himself
of his financial holdings

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.240
and a logistics company that does business

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.280
with the postal service.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.270
He also went out and
purchased Amazon stock

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.089
after his nomination as postmaster general

00:10:13.089 --> 00:10:16.580
which is a potential red flag
for conflict of interest.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.300
And speaking of Amazon,

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.920
the company does have a
great deal with the USPS.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.773
The retail giant focuses
its own delivery network

00:10:22.773 --> 00:10:26.590
on densely populated urban
areas which keeps its costs low.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:28.780
However, this means
that the postal service

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.640
which is required to serve everyone

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.170
effectively winds up
subsidizing Amazon delivery

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.100
to low population density areas.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.100
The address is that it
wouldn't be profitable

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:40.050
for Amazon to deliver
to which coincidentally

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:44.120
are very, very red counties
across the country.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.650
And ironically Republicans,
including President Trump

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:49.500
have criticized the Amazon
deal as being bad for business.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.780
And in spite of or perhaps
because of this relationship

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:54.441
with Amazon, President Trump has disagreed

00:10:54.441 --> 00:10:57.550
with various Democratic
proposals to increase funding

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.770
for the post office.

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:01.452
So let's talk about the recent
changes that DeJoy brought

00:11:01.452 --> 00:11:03.300
to the US postal service.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.480
On July 10th, DeJoy announced
a major operational pivot

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:09.630
which imposes new significant
restrictions on the timing

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.720
and nature of letter carrier routes.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.770
DeJoy admitted that
this would cause delays

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.560
in the memo where he said,
we may see mail left behind

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.870
or mail on the workroom
floor which is not typical.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:21.740
And just to be clear, DeJoy also says

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:24.560
he didn't make any of these
controversial changes.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:26.780
- Could you please tell me
who did order these changes

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.923
if you as postmaster general did not?

00:11:28.923 --> 00:11:33.923
- There were many, many executives
almost 30,000 executives

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.777
within the organization.

00:11:35.777 --> 00:11:39.330
And there were plans that
existed prior to my arrival

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:41.510
that will continue that were implemented.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.080
- But postal workers have been trained

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.240
not to leave letters
behind, make multiple trips

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.450
to ensure timely distribution of the mail.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.900
This is why they sometimes
make unscheduled deliveries

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:51.530
or deliver mail on a Sunday.

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.744
DeJoy now says that carriers
leave this mail behind

00:11:53.744 --> 00:11:56.300
for the next day which
may accumulate and pile up

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.630
as time goes on.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:59.610
In addition, letter
carriers are now prohibited

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:01.190
from sorting mail in the morning

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.710
and delivering it in the afternoon.

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:04.730
Instead, they will get
to the routes earlier

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.330
in the morning and then
return to their posts

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.020
to sort mail in the afternoon.

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:11.720
And some of these policies
directly effect ballot delivery.

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:14.300
On July 29th, the USPS
general council announced

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.740
a policy change directly
targeting balance.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.440
Letters said that the ballot
sent by marketing mail

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:21.750
would not be accorded
first class mail treatment

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.680
and thus take longer to deliver.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.660
The postal service had
previously trained as employees

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:27.440
to give first-class treatment to balance

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:29.490
in any other election related materials

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.240
sent as marketing mail.

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:34.360
This change imposes much bigger
financial burdens on states

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.970
which will now have to
pay 55 cents per piece

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:39.680
for first class delivery rather
than the 20 cents per piece

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.000
they previously paid.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.180
States are already
anticipating huge increases

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:44.220
in requests for ballots.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:46.440
This comes at a time when state budgets

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.850
are completely in shambles
because of COVID-19.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:51.130
In addition, postal clerks
can no longer provide

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.750
a witness signature on balance

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.720
and some states you need
a third party witness

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:56.400
when you sign a mailed ballot.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.290
And the ballots typically say that voters

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.590
can simply go to the post office

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.430
and have a worker watch them sign

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:04.020
that this practice is now ended.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.780
And one of the most baffling measures

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:08.030
has been the decommissioning of 10%

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:10.950
of the mail sorting machines
at postal service centers.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.990
These machines can sort 30,000
pieces of mail per hour.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.330
And although DeJoy said that
he would stop doing this,

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:19.050
they've already decommissioned
95% of the machines

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.820
that were planned to be disconnected.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.670
In August DeJoy ordered the postal service

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.880
to remove 671 mail sorting
machines by the end of September

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:30.090
including 24 in Ohio, 11
in Detroit, 11 in Florida,

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.060
nine in Wisconsin, eight in Philadelphia

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:33.540
and five in Arizona.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.020
What's interesting about these states

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.860
is that these just happened to be states

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:38.880
which are expected to decide the outcome

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.440
of the presidential election.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:42.910
And DeJoy who claims he
didn't make these changes

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:46.140
has a firm opinion on whether
he would ever reverse them.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:51.140
- Mr. DeJoy will you commit
to reversing these changes?

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:52.583
- No.

00:13:52.583 --> 00:13:54.930
- These actions have already
spurred nationwide mail delays

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.220
in mail collection, mail
sorting and mail delivery.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.970
And a mail processing facility
in Santa Clarita in July,

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:02.290
workers discovered that their
automated sorting machines

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:04.150
had been disabled and padlocked.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.580
At a large mail sorting
facility in Los Angeles,

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:07.920
workers told the LA Times

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.150
that they are so far
behind processing packages

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:13.160
that by early August, nats
and rodents were swarming

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.430
around containers of
rotted fruit and meat.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.068
And a brief warning to animal lovers,

00:14:17.068 --> 00:14:20.150
there were even some packages
containing small animals

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:22.090
which perished in their boxes.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.640
In Southeast Washington DC,

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:25.810
residents have gone weeks
without receiving any mail.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.732
- People have medical supplies

00:14:27.732 --> 00:14:29.890
that are delivered by the mail.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.820
They have utility bills,

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:34.670
they have important financial documents.

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.290
- Which they are not receiving

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.120
and I can say personally
that one of the mailboxes

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:42.880
that has been in my own
neighborhood in Washington DC

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.740
which has been there
for years if not decades

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:48.270
was recently removed just a few weeks ago

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:50.620
and I've never received
an explanation why.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:52.660
There've been many reports of veterans

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.200
and elderly citizens who
rely on mail delivery

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.290
of their medication, going through delays

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.470
and entire native American
tribes in California

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:02.620
haven't received mail for weeks.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.760
So not surprisingly, this
has created all kinds

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:05.830
of legal battles.

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:08.310
Voters, states, advocacy
groups and candidates

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:10.200
are suing the Trump
administration over changes

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.300
at the postal service.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:14.390
The NAACP filed a lawsuit
against DeJoy and Trump,

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:16.260
the NAACP is main cause of action

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:17.530
is that the postal service ignored

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:19.780
the postal reorganization act by failing

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.470
to seek an advisory opinion from the PRC

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:26.750
under 39 USC section 3661
before implementing changes

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:28.971
that have a nationwide
impact on mail delivery.

00:15:28.971 --> 00:15:31.610
The postal service has
to provide an opportunity

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.080
for public comment and
seek in advisory opinion

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:35.710
from the postal rate commission.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.220
The opinion may not issue
until the commission provides

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.940
an opportunity for public hearing.

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:42.460
And here it's undisputed that
the postal service failed

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.320
to do so with respect to either the pivot

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.050
or the change in treatment of ballots sent

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:47.180
by marketing mail.

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:48.440
And Congress also mandates

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:49.820
that the postal service shall give

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:51.570
the highest consideration
to the requirement

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.419
for the most expeditious
collection, transportation

00:15:53.419 --> 00:15:56.220
and delivery of important letter mail.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.246
The NAACP argues that the
postal services reversal

00:15:58.246 --> 00:16:00.849
of its policy of according
first class service

00:16:00.849 --> 00:16:03.880
to ballots sent by marketing
mail is inconsistent

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:05.480
with that statutory mandate.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.330
And it's also obvious

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.900
that DeJoy's changes violated the APA.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.290
The biggest question is
whether a court will order him

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.680
to reverse course and remediate the steps

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:14.900
that have already been taken.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.570
Others argue that this
violates the elections clause

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:19.850
and the electors clause
of the constitution.

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:21.960
Pennsylvania, Maine, California, Delaware,

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.330
the District of Columbia,
Massachusetts and North Carolina

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.237
have filed a lawsuit against
the federal government

00:16:26.237 --> 00:16:29.220
raising many of the same
claims as the NAACP.

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:31.570
In addition, the state's
alleged that DeJoy actions

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:34.210
are unconstitutional under
the elections clause.

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.740
The constitution elections
clause vests authority

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:39.060
in the states to regulate
the quote time place

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.340
and manner of holding
elections for senators

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.840
and representatives that
will represent the state.

00:16:43.840 --> 00:16:46.070
But only Congress may displace how a state

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:47.620
has chosen to regulate the time place

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.280
and manner of a federal election.

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:51.740
The constitution electors
clause vest authority

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.013
in the states to a point, quote,

00:16:53.013 --> 00:16:55.277
" A number of electors
equal to the whole number

00:16:55.277 --> 00:16:57.967
"of senators and representatives
to which the state

00:16:57.967 --> 00:17:00.260
"may be entitled in Congress."

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.550
The plaintiff's states here
alleged they've exercised

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.800
these rights by expanding voting by mail.

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:07.260
When they pass legislation
that expanded vote by mail,

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.640
they relied on the postal
services long history

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:12.180
in delivering election
mail in a timely manner.

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:15.060
They contend that DeJoy
abrupt changes interfere

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.630
with the constitutional
power given to the states

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:17.819
to control their own elections

00:17:17.819 --> 00:17:20.220
and other alleged violations of the first

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.640
and 14th amendments.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.445
Certain voters have the
Trump administration

00:17:23.445 --> 00:17:26.410
and DeJoy actions arguing
that they are being denied

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:27.277
their right to vote.

00:17:27.277 --> 00:17:28.820
And these suits the plaintiff's alleged

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:31.215
that the way DeJoy is
managing the postal service

00:17:31.215 --> 00:17:33.310
will stop some voters from voting at all

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:35.190
which would be a severe burden.

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:37.240
Plaintiffs include people
who have medical conditions

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.240
that make COVID-19 especially dangerous

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.180
and people who live in remote areas

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.352
and cannot travel long
distances to vote in person.

00:17:43.352 --> 00:17:46.330
And theoretically, if a
burden would essentially deny

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.790
a person in the right to vote,
then it could be considered

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.688
though others would argue that
everyone faces some burden

00:17:52.688 --> 00:17:55.820
in voting, it's simply a spectrum here.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.750
But the plaintiffs in these
suits say that the government

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:59.440
doesn't have any real estate interest

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:00.950
in making the dramatic changes.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.840
And the only interest
that postmaster DeJoy

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:05.450
has identified as cost
saving and efficiency.

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:07.490
Plaintiffs argue that while cost saving

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:10.620
is important in government in
many ways, it's settled law

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.340
that constitutional rights
cannot be taken away

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.260
because it's too expensive to grant them.

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.539
In addition, the postal services mandate

00:18:15.539 --> 00:18:18.670
to serve as an affordable
public service seems to clash

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:21.000
with the idea that
cost-savings should interfere

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.300
with constitutional rights.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.310
The plaintiffs also note

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:24.890
that the president stated justification

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:28.203
for denying post office funding
his own political fortunes

00:18:28.203 --> 00:18:30.980
is obviously not the kind of
legitimate government interest

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:33.540
that would justify a burden
on voters and candidates.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.670
But some of the damage
has already been done

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.580
and unfortunately, the courts
will be relatively slow to act

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.350
and reports continue
that the postal service

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:42.710
